  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobility and needs monitoring &#x2013; displacement tracking matrix for the Syrian Arab Republic</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM through CERF is proposing to contribute to a comprehensive and integrated humanitarian intervention, allowing the most urgent and pressing needs to be addressed swiftly by providing evidence base to guide responses. The main objective is to ensure dignified, safe, and secure living conditions, along with basic services for vulnerable populations affected by the ongoing humanitarian crisis in Syria. IOM thus proposes a twofold response including I) Country-wide needs identification, including in hard-to-reach areas); and II) Well-coordinated multisectoral response by OCHA and partners to support the most vulnerable conflict affected populations.</narrative>
  </description>
